  "$comment": "2026-10-03: Four added critical cells own legacy schema persistence, normalization, linear indexing and bounded population/teardown. Their 95/100/95 values are explicit acceptance targets, not a claimed complete coverage measurement. All existing floors and global/diff controls stay unchanged; full coverage of the final integrated source remains required. 2026-10-04: MergeNeed owns successful population reuse and retry eligibility for later accepted updates. Real same-locale relationship-change failures exposed an untested cache-validity gap; add its 100/100/100 acceptance target without changing existing global, diff or file floors. This scope addition does not claim measured coverage. 2026-10-24: these acceptance targets are enforced: vitest.config.ts spreads every criticalFiles entry into the coverage thresholds, so the Coverage job fails below them on every push. 2026-10-26 (2.2 review): src/runtime/inline/generator.ts and src/tools/doctor/readiness.ts become critical files, and with that part of the nightly mutation scope. The generator writes the configuration every adapter page runs on, and a silent mistake there (a gate threshold of Infinity serialized as null) reached every such page; readiness.ts reads the configuration a served page carries and decides LP0705 and LP0709. Measured: generator.ts 100/100/100, readiness.ts 100 % of lines and functions and 95.56 % of branches (86 of 90; two are the unreachable `?? ''` fallbacks of the tuple reader). The floors are those values, rounded down. 2026-11-24: three modules that were logic inside a barrel until that day become critical files, and with that part of the nightly mutation scope: `src/runtime/client/live-preview-client.ts` (the programmatic client), `src/server/payload/live-preview-url.ts` (the URL the admin frames) and `src/runtime/fragment/strategy.ts` (beside the five fragment modules already here). Coverage never measured them while they were `index.ts`. Measured with 6,379 tests: the client 69 of 71 lines (97.18 %), 29 of 29 functions, 41 of 42 branches (97.62 %); the two lines are the catch of `destroy()`. The other two 100 % of lines, functions and branches. The floors are those values, rounded down. 2026-11-24 (O-56): `src/adapters/shared/fragment-endpoint.ts` is split, and its two new neighbours are critical files like it: `fragment-request-scope.ts` holds the lifetime of an accepted request, `fragment-request-body.ts` the bounded body read. Measured with 6,372 tests: the endpoint 86 of 86 lines, 13 of 13 functions, 111 of 112 branches (99.11 %); the body reader 74 of 74 lines, 12 of 13 functions (92.31 %), 42 of 44 branches (95.45 %); the request scope 100 % of lines, functions and branches. The floors are those values, rounded down; the endpoint's own floor rises from 97/97/93, which had been measured over the unsplit file. 2026-11-28 (3.0, ADR 0007 row 47): `core/strategies/lent-route.ts` is critical: it decides whether a page's route is refreshed through the lent refresh alone, which since row 47 is every page a framework hydrates. Measured 100 % of 7 lines, 4 functions and 11 branches. 2026-11-28 (3.0, the domains under src/ sit in four zones): the exclusions of client/config.ts and codegen/cli.ts follow their files into `src/runtime` and `src/tools`, which the ratchet reads off the rename as it does for a baseline. The exclusion of the generated runtime is removed: since no generated file is committed on the 3.0 line it is ignored by git, and the changed-line gate lists tracked files and untracked ones git does not ignore, so the entry matched nothing. 2026-11-28 (3.0, the three runtime files at the 600-line cap are cut): four modules that took code out of critical files are critical themselves, so no line leaves the floor it was under: `core/strategies/route-run.ts` (from `strategy-runner.ts`; measured 95.23 % of lines, every function, 91.83 % of branches), `core/session/cache-rebuild.ts` and `core/session/refused-message.ts` (from `lifecycle.ts`; every line and function, 78.26 % and 100 % of branches) and `core/update/after-flush.ts` (from `update-pipeline.ts`; every line and function, 90 % of branches). The floors are those values, rounded down; the three files they came from keep theirs."
